  "leg_joint_discs": "solid discs from the still's own pixels on BOTH plates of each leg joint: knee r=34 seed px (7 px into the cuisse, 3625 into the greave), ankle r=34 (2019 into the greave, 657 into the sabaton). Matching discs about a shared pivot cannot be separated by a rotation about it.",
  "leg_near_thigh_knee": "cuisse extended over the greave by 298 px (seed rows 995..1064) -- the union, over the knee's -6..+88 deg working range, of the pixels the poleyn seam leaves bare; painted with the still's own pixels at those coordinates.",
  "leg_near_thigh": "hip end grown into a SOLID DISC of radius 38 seed px centred on the hip socket (438, 830) (6009 px filled), painted from the cuisse's own widest plate band, tiled vertically and clamped to the nearest column with plate. A disc centred on the pivot is invariant under rotation about it, so the socket stays covered at every angle of the walk and the run -- this replaces a rectangular clone_up whose corners swung clear of the socket and let the thigh read as detached.",
  "arm_near_lo": "couter end cloned 14 rows upward -- the upper arm is behind the surcoat in the still",
